This hackathon-prep pack aggregates content under several upstream licenses.
Each third-party file or asset retains its original license; see per-file
license headers and the file `assets/LICENSES.md` for the authoritative
source-by-source attribution. Summary:

- MIT: hand-authored files in this prep pack
       (JamKitParticleFactory.cs, JamKit_MinimalInputActions.inputactions,
        RECIPES.md, INTEGRATION.md, README.md, OPEN-ASSETS.md, plus this
        LICENSE), and third-party MIT-licensed content (LitMotion, Boost
        SuccessParticles.prefab, Bfxr2).
- BSD-3-Clause: jfxr.
- CC0: Kenney asset packs (UI Pack, Particle Pack, Interface Sounds, Impact
       Sounds, Fantasy UI Borders, etc.), OpenGameArt music tracks, the
       ChipTone output.
- SIL OFL 1.1: Roboto-LICENSE.txt, Inter-LICENSE.txt, PressStart2P-LICENSE.txt,
       BebasNeue-LICENSE.txt (each ships alongside its .ttf).
- Apache 2.0: Roboto (Apache 2.0; Roboto-LICENSE.txt + Roboto-NOTICE.txt
       ship alongside the .ttf).
- zlib: rFXGen.
- Unity Companion License (UCL): `JamKit_DefaultInputActions.inputactions`
       (derived from `Unity-Technologies/InputSystem` DefaultInputActions),
       `JamKit_URP_PostProcessing_Profile.asset` (derived from
       `Unity-Technologies/UniversalRenderingExamples` FPS Post-process
       Volume Profile), `CinemachineSampleSceneProfile_URP.asset` (derived
       from `Unity-Technologies/com.unity.cinemachine` URP sample), and the
       `_URPExamples_source_*` / `_Cinemachine_source_*` reference files.
       Full UCL §5 Notices text is reproduced in `assets/LICENSES.md` §
       "Unity Companion License note (G2, G3) — Compliance statement".

For the complete source-by-source attribution table, see `assets/LICENSES.md`.